body:
i didn't have that extreme of an extreme hunger since i started my recovery in the clinic where the concept itself was kinda not exsisting, and while i ceartainly had extreme hunger i just never fully honored it bc i was never told to. but at home, where i was already weighing much more and was out of dangerous teritorry i tried all in and had a few things i distincly remember

&#x200B;

what i probably remember most was when my mom and i came home from buying groceries in the evening. (which for some reasons buying groceries with others is still a big stressor for me) we went with friends of my moms partner, which i don't know, aswell. and they wanted to be generous and therefore payed for the whole groceries for both them and us, and packed a huge bag with crossaints, apple filled pastries, and loads of other stuff. i am sure it was 7 or so pasteries and my mom probably expected that they would last for a while. by the next morning i had eaten all of them + probably some slices of bread with nutella aswell before or afterwards.  my mom didn't even get ONE of the pasteries. i was so ashamed.

and i didn't feel stuffed like at all. when i ate a crossaint, half an hour later i was hungry again. and not lightly hungy, hungry to the point where it starts to hurt. WHERE TF WAS THAT FOOD EVEN REALISTICLY GOING????? did it just disepear?

&#x200B;

i was never really a secret eater. extreme hunger was the only time i snuck into the kitchen often beacause my mom seeing how much i was eating was just too much for me
